## 1. Introduction

This guide covers the creation and implementation of forms using the uu5 framework. Forms are essential components for collecting user input and should follow specific patterns and best practices.

### 1.1 When to Use

Use this guide when:
- Creating forms for user input collection
- Implementing validation logic
- Building complex multi-field forms
- Working with form layouts and styling

For detailed form component implementation patterns, see [Form Component Guide](mdc:docs/uu5/form-component-guide.md).

## 2. Form Structure

### 2.1 Overview

### 2.2 Basic Components
Forms consist of three main component types:

1. **Form Component** - Covers inputs and controls, collects data from inputs, stores them in state and validates them
2. **Inputs** - Fields for getting data from user that automatically communicate with form
3. **Controls** - Buttons for working with form (submitting, resetting, validating, etc.)

### 2.3 Form Props
Standard form props include:
- `onSubmit` - Function to handle form submission (can be synchronous or asynchronous)
- `gridLayout` - Layout configuration for form inputs
- `onValidate` - Custom validation function
- `layout` - Layout configuration
- `size` - Size of form elements
- `borderRadius` - Border radius styling
- `readOnly` - Read-only state
- `disabled` - Disabled state
- `id`, `className`, `style` - Standard styling props
- `elementAttrs`, `elementRef`, `noIndex` - Additional props

### 2.4 Input Props
Each form input supports:

**Standard input props:**
- `name` - required
- `initialValue`
- `required`
- `disabled` and `readOnly` - not available for Checkbox, Checkboxes, Radios, SwitchSelect
- `placeholder`

**Validation props:**
- `validateOnChange`

**Visual props:**
- `label`, `info`, `message`
- `size`, `layout`, `borderRadius`

**Other props:**
- `id`, `className`, `style`
- `elementAttrs`, `elementRef`, `noIndex`
- `onValidate` - Custom validation function

## 3. Implementation Guidelines

### 3.1 Basic Form Creation
```javascript
<Uu5Forms.Form
  gridLayout="name, note"
  onSubmit={async (e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    // TODO some call to server for storing data
  }}
>
  <Uu5Forms.FormText name="name" label="Name" required />
  <Uu5Forms.FormTextArea name="note" label="Note" />
  <Uu5Forms.SubmitButton
    className={Config.Css.css({ justifySelf: "end" })}
  />
</Uu5Forms.Form>
```

### 3.2 LSI (Localization) Usage
All text properties (`label`, `info`, `placeholder`, `message`) automatically accept LSI objects:

```javascript
<Uu5Forms.FormText
  name="name"
  label={{ en: "Name", cs: "Jméno" }}
  info={{
    en: "You can find your name on your ID card.",
    cs: "Své jméno najdete v občaském průkazu.",
  }}
  placeholder={{ en: "John Smith", cs: "Jan Novák" }}
  message={{ en: "Name and surname", cs: "Jméno a příjmení" }}
  required
/>
```

**Note:** All properties except `placeholder` also accept React components for complex content.

## 4. Validation

### 4.1 Input Validation
```javascript
<Uu5Forms.FormNumber
  name="count"
  label="Count"
  initialValue={1}
  required
  min={1}
  max={5}
  message="Item count is limited by current stock reserve."
  onValidate={async (e) => {
    const { value } = e.data;
    const { maxAvailable } = await Calls.getItemAvailability();
    if (value > maxAvailable) {
      return {
        feedback: "error",
        messageParams: [maxAvailable],
        message: {
          en: "Unfortunately, %d items are currently available.",
        },
      };
    }
  }}
/>
```

### 4.2 Form Validation
```javascript
<Uu5Forms.Form
  gridLayout="count, color"
  onSubmit={(e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    // TODO some call to server for storing data
  }}
  onValidate={async (e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    const { count, color } = values;
    const { maxAvailable } = await Calls.checkItemAvailability(values);
    if (count > maxAvailable) {
      return {
        feedback: "error",
        messageParams: [maxAvailable, color],
        message: {
          en: "Unfortunately, %s %s items are currently available.",
        },
      };
    }
  }}
>
  {/* form inputs */}
</Uu5Forms.Form>
```

## 5. Layout Configuration

### 5.1 Grid Layout
Use `gridLayout` for simple form layouting:

```javascript
<Uu5Forms.Form
  gridLayout={{
    xs: "firstName, surname, note, submit",
    m: "firstName note, surname note, submit submit"
  }}
  onSubmit={(e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    // TODO some call to server for storing data
  }}
>
  <Uu5Forms.FormText
    name="firstName"
    label="Name"
    required
    style={{ gridArea: "firstName" }}
  />
  <Uu5Forms.FormText
    name="surname"
    label="Surname"
    required
    style={{ gridArea: "surname" }}
  />
  <Uu5Forms.FormTextArea
    name="note"
    label="Note"
    style={{ gridArea: "note" }}
  />
  <Uu5Forms.SubmitButton
    name="submit"
    className={Config.Css.css({ justifySelf: "end" })}
  />
</Uu5Forms.Form>
```

### 5.2 Form Layout Props
Set layout properties on the form to apply to all inputs:

```javascript
<Uu5Forms.Form
  gridLayout="firstName, surname, note"
  size="xl"
  layout="1:2"
  borderRadius="full"
  onSubmit={async (e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    // TODO some call to server for storing data
  }}
>
  <Uu5Forms.FormText name="firstName" label="Name" required />
  <Uu5Forms.FormText name="surname" label="Surname" required />
  <Uu5Forms.FormTextArea name="note" label="Note" />
  <Uu5Forms.SubmitButton
    className={Config.Css.css({ justifySelf: "end" })}
  />
</Uu5Forms.Form>
```

## 6. Best Practices

### 6.1 Form Structure
- Always use the Form component as the wrapper
- Use appropriate input components for data types
- Include proper validation
- Use LSI for all user-facing text

### 6.2 Validation
- Use native validation props when possible (`min`, `max`, `pattern`, etc.)
- Implement custom validation for business logic
- Provide clear error messages
- Use both synchronous and asynchronous validation as needed

### 6.3 Layout
- Use `gridLayout` for responsive form layout
- Set layout properties on the form to apply to all inputs
- Use appropriate sizing and spacing
- Consider different screen sizes in layout configuration

### 6.4 Accessibility
- Always provide meaningful labels
- Use `required` prop for mandatory fields
- Provide helpful info and message text
- Ensure proper form structure

### 6.5 Performance
- Use async validation sparingly
- Implement proper error handling
- Consider form state management for complex forms

### 6.6 Common Form Inputs

**Text Inputs:**
- `FormText` - Single line text
- `FormTextArea` - Multi-line text
- `FormPassword` - Password input
- `FormNumber` - Numeric input
- `FormDate` - Date input

**Selection Inputs:**
- `FormSelect` - Dropdown selection
- `FormSwitchSelect` - Switch-based selection
- `FormCheckbox` - Single checkbox
- `FormCheckboxes` - Multiple checkboxes
- `FormRadios` - Radio button group

**Other Inputs:**
- `FormFile` - File upload
- `FormSlider` - Range slider
- `FormSwitch` - Toggle switch

## 7. Troubleshooting

### 7.1 Error Handling

**Validation Errors:**
- Return validation objects with `feedback: "error"`
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Use `messageParams` for dynamic content
- Support LSI for error messages

**Form Submission Errors:**
- Handle async operations in `onSubmit`
- Provide user feedback for submission status
- Implement proper error recovery

### 7.2 Testing

**Unit Tests:**
- Test form validation logic
- Test form submission
- Test error handling
- Test accessibility features

**Integration Tests:**
- Test complete form workflows
- Test with different data scenarios
- Test responsive behavior
- Test with various user interactions

### 7.3 Examples

**Simple Contact Form:**
```javascript
<Uu5Forms.Form
  gridLayout="name, email, message, submit"
  onSubmit={async (e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    await Calls.submitContactForm(values);
  }}
>
  <Uu5Forms.FormText
    name="name"
    label="Full Name"
    required
  />
  <Uu5Forms.FormText
    name="email"
    label="Email"
    type="email"
    required
  />
  <Uu5Forms.FormTextArea
    name="message"
    label="Message"
    required
  />
  <Uu5Forms.SubmitButton />
</Uu5Forms.Form>
```

**Complex Form with Validation:**
```javascript
<Uu5Forms.Form
  gridLayout="product, quantity, color, submit"
  onSubmit={async (e) => {
    const values = e.data.value;
    await Calls.createOrder(values);
  }}
  onValidate={async (e) => {
    const { product, quantity } = e.data.value;
    const availability = await Calls.checkAvailability(product);
    if (quantity > availability) {
      return {
        feedback: "error",
        message: "Insufficient stock available"
      };
    }
  }}
>
  <Uu5Forms.FormSelect
    name="product"
    label="Product"
    itemList={productOptions}
    required
  />
  <Uu5Forms.FormNumber
    name="quantity"
    label="Quantity"
    min={1}
    max={10}
    required
  />
  <Uu5Forms.FormSwitchSelect
    name="color"
    label="Color"
    itemList={colorOptions}
    required
  />
  <Uu5Forms.SubmitButton />
</Uu5Forms.Form>
```

**Form in Modal:**
```javascript
//@@viewOn:imports
import { createVisualComponent, createComponent, useState } from "uu5g05";
import Uu5Forms from "uu5g05-forms";
import Uu5Elements from "uu5g05-elements";
import Config from "./config/config.js";
//@@viewOff:imports

const BuyModal = createVisualComponent({
  //@@viewOn:statics
  uu5Tag: Config.TAG + "BuyModal",
  //@@viewOff:statics

  render(props) {
    //@@viewOn:private
    let deliveryDateMin = new UuDate();
    deliveryDateMin.setDay(deliveryDateMin.getDay() + 3, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    //@@viewOff:private

    //@@viewOn:render
    return (
      <Uu5Forms.Form.Provider
        onSubmit={(e) => {
          if (!navigator.onLine) throw new Error("Demo submit error example.");
          alert("Submitted with values:\n" + JSON.stringify(e.data.value, null, 2));
          props.onClose();
        }}
      >
        {({ cancel }) => (
          <Uu5Elements.Modal
            {...props}
            onClose={async () => {
              const leave = await cancel();
              if (leave) props.onClose();
            }}
            header="Buy a T-shirt"
            info="Buy a Red Monster T-shirt in a limited edition and win one of interesting presents."
            footer={
              <Uu5Elements.Grid
                templateColumns={{ xs: "repeat(2, 1fr)", s: "repeat(2, auto)" }}
                columnGap={Uu5Elements.UuGds.SpacingPalette.getValue(["fixed", "c"])}
                justifyContent={{ s: "end" }}
              >
                <Uu5Forms.CancelButton onClick={props.onClose} />
                <Uu5Forms.SubmitButton>Buy</Uu5Forms.SubmitButton>
              </Uu5Elements.Grid>
            }
          >
            <Uu5Forms.Form.View>
              <div
                className={Config.Css.css({
                  display: "grid",
                  rowGap: 8,
                  columnGap: 32,
                  gridAutoFlow: "column",
                  gridTemplateRows: "repeat(4, auto)",
                  marginBottom: 8,
                })}
              >
                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormRadios
                    name="sex"
                    label="Gender"
                    itemList={[
                      { value: "man", children: "For Man" },
                      { value: "woman", children: "For Woman" },
                    ]}
                    required
                  />
                </div>

                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormSwitchSelect
                    name="size"
                    label="Size"
                    initialValue="M"
                    itemList={[{ value: "S" }, { value: "M" }, { value: "L" }, { value: "XL" }, { value: "XXL" }]}
                  />
                </div>

                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormNumber
                    name="count"
                    label="Item count"
                    required
                    min={1}
                    initialValue={1}
                    message="Item count is limited by current stock reserve."
                    onValidate={async (e) => {
                      const { value } = e.data;
                      const { maxAvailable } = await Calls.getItemAvailability();
                      if (value > maxAvailable) {
                        return {
                          messageParams: [maxAvailable],
                          message: {
                            en: "Unfortunately, only %d items are currently available.",
                          },
                        };
                      }
                    }}
                  />
                </div>

                <div className={Config.Css.css({ display: "grid", rowGap: 8 })}>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormSelect
                    name="destination"
                    label="Destination"
                    initialValue="prague"
                    itemList={[
                      { value: "prague", children: "Prague" },
                      { value: "plzen", children: "Plzeň" },
                      { value: "hk", children: "Hradec Králové" },
                      { value: "brno", children: "Brno" },
                      { value: "bratislava", children: "Bratislava" },
                      { value: "kosice", children: "Košice" },
                      { value: "kyiv", children: "Kyiv" },
                      { value: "ternopil", children: "Ternopil" },
                    ]}
                  />

                  <Uu5Forms.FormDate
                    name="deliveryDate"
                    label="Preferred delivery date"
                    min={deliveryDateMin.toIsoString()}
                  />
                </div>

                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormText name="name" label="Name" placeholder="Name and surname" required />
                </div>
                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormText
                    name="phone"
                    label="Phone"
                    iconLeft="uugds-phone"
                    prefix="+420"
                    type="tel"
                    required
                  />
                </div>
                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormEmail name="email" label="E-mail" required />
                </div>
                <div>
                  <Uu5Forms.FormTextArea name="desc" label="Notes" />
                </div>
              </div>

              <Uu5Forms.FormCheckbox
                name="conditions"
                label={
                  <>
                    I agree to <Uu5Elements.Link>Terms and conditions</Uu5Elements.Link>
                  </>
                }
                required
              />
            </Uu5Forms.Form.View>
          </Uu5Elements.Modal>
        )}
      </Uu5Forms.Form.Provider>
    );
    //@@viewOff:render
  },
});

const Page = createComponent({
  render() {
    //@@viewOn:private
    const [modalOpen, setModalOpen] = useState(false);
    //@@viewOff:private

    //@@viewOn:render
    return (
      <div>
        <Uu5Elements.Button onClick={() => setModalOpen(true)}>Buy a T-shirt</Uu5Elements.Button>
        <BuyModal open={modalOpen} onClose={() => setModalOpen(false)} />
      </div>
    );
    //@@viewOff:render
  },
});
```

### 7.4 ESLint Fix
> After completing all testing and validation, you MUST run eslint fix to resolve any linting errors:
> 
> **Run ESLint Fix**:
> ```bash
> # Option 1: Direct eslint command
> npx eslint src/ --fix
> 
> # Option 2: Using project-specific eslint config
> npx eslint "src/**/*.js" --fix
> ```
> 
> **Verify ESLint Results**:
> - Check that all linting errors are resolved
> - Ensure code follows project style guidelines
> - Verify no new warnings are introduced
> - Confirm all files pass linting checks
> 
> **If ESLint errors persist**:
> - Review and fix any remaining manual errors
> - Check for configuration issues
> - Ensure all imports and dependencies are correct
> - Re-run eslint fix until all errors are resolved
> 
> **Purpose**: Ensures the form component code follows project standards and is free of linting errors before completion.

